	(text "HAT SIGNALS  (owner: Ibrahim). This file is yours. Draw between the labels: left = from the Pi, right = out to the drivers.\nDon't rename or delete a label. They match the pins on the root page. Ask Eeshan if you need a new one.\n\nWHAT GOES ON THIS SHEET (full pin numbers: the notes on the Pi header sheet and README.md)\n  1. Buffer: symbol 74xx:74AHCT244 (same pinout), set its value to 74ACT244.  1A1-1A3 / 2A1-2A3 from the PUL, DIR, ENA labels,\n      1Y1-1Y3 / 2Y1-2Y3 to the *_DRV_* labels.  1OE + 2OE = BUF_OE_N with a 10k pull-up to +3V3.\n      VCC = +5V with a 100 nF cap to GND.  Unused inputs 1A4 and 2A4 to GND.\n  2. J301 / J302 (ALT / AZ driver terminals: 5V / PUL- / DIR- / ENA-) are placed already, because they anchor the cable\n      to the power sheet. Wire 1Y1-1Y3 / 2Y1-2Y3 onto their *_DRV_* wires and pick their screw-terminal footprint.\n  3. Limit switches: a connector per switch, 10k pull-up to +3V3 and 100 nF to GND on each line. Switch NC contact goes to GND.\n  4. Encoders: connector spots only (nothing bought yet). The Pi takes 3.3V max.\n  5. Give every part a footprint. Inspect > Electrical Rules Checker: 0 errors before you open a pull request.\nThe 'unconnected wire end' warnings on the short label wires go away once you wire to them."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.4 22.86 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "27755842-afe9-59c6-a800-ef281865158d")
	)
